== problems
== relational schema
Relational schema
Notation: _name_ primary key, /name/ foreign key, _/name/_ both

HR:
  Member : {(_/PersonID/_ : integer, SocialSecurityNbr : string, HouseNbr : string, Street : string, PostalCode : integer, Region : string, Function : string, Password : string, Authorization : string)}
  InventoryMgmt.Team : {(_TeamID_ : integer, Name : string)}
  Member_partOf_InventoryMgmt.Team : {(_/PersonID/_ : integer, _/TeamID/_ : integer)}
  InventoryMgmt.Team_updates_SaleInventoryItem : {(_/TeamID/_ : integer, _/ItemID/_ : integer)}
LoggingSubdomain:
  LogEntry : {(_SessionID_ : integer, Date : date, Time : time, ActionType : string, /concernsPersonID/ : integer, /performedByPersonID/ : integer, /clientID/ : integer, /InvoiceNbr/ : string, /DateOfIssue/ : date, /BookingID/ : integer, /ArticleCode/ : integer)}
  LogDetail : {(_DetailSq_ : string, FieldName : string, OldValue : string, NewValue : string, /SessionID/ : integer)}
Inventory:
  SaleUnit : {(_ArticleCode_ : integer, Name : string, WholesalerPurchasePrice : decimal, ShopperSalePrice : decimal, MerchantSalePrice : decimal, category : string)}
  SpecialOffer : {(_/ArticleCode/_ : integer, IncludedItemsCount : integer)}
  Article : {(_/ArticleCode/_ : integer)}
  SaleInventoryItem : {(_ItemID_ : integer, Name : string, StockCount : integer, Weight : float, Size : float)}
  SpecialCondition : {(_ConditionID_ : integer, Description : string, ConditionType : string, ConditionValue : string)}
  SaleInventoryItem_partOf_SaleUnit : {(_/ItemID/_ : integer, _/ArticleCode/_ : integer)}
  SpecialOffer_requires_SpecialCondition : {(_/ArticleCode/_ : integer, _/ConditionID/_ : integer)}
Customers:
  Client : {(_clientID_ : integer, CreditRating : string, EmailAddress : string, category : string)}
  Shopper : {(_/PersonID/_ : integer, aaa : string, /clientID/ : integer)}
  Merchant : {(_/clientID/_ : integer, MerchantID : integer, SectorOfTrade : string)}
  CreditCard : {(_CardNbr_ : string, ValidityDate : date, /clientID/ : integer)}
  PhoneContact : {(_ContactID_ : integer, PhoneNbr : string, /clientID/ : integer)}
Sales:
  PurchaseOrder : {(_BookingID_ : integer, DeliveryDate : date, DeliveryAddress : string, Password : string, DeliveryInstructions : string, /InvoiceNbr/ : string, /DateOfIssue/ : date)}
  Invoice : {(_InvoiceNbr_ : string, _DateOfIssue_ : date, TimeForPayment : decimal, TimeOfPayment : decimal)}
  CreditCardOpt. : {(_/OptionID/_ : integer, /CardNbr/ : string)}
  PayOnDeliveryOpt. : {(_/OptionID/_ : integer, /ContactID/ : integer)}
  PaymentOption : {(_OptionID_ : integer, category : string)}
  SalesDiscount : {(_/BookingID/_ : integer, _DiscountPosition_ : string, Amount : decimal, Type(abs.|Rel.) : string)}
  BookingItem : {(_/BookingID/_ : integer, _PositionNbr_ : string, Quantity : integer, UnitPriceAtPurchase : string, /ArticleCode/ : integer)}
  chooses : {(/BookingID/ : integer, _/OptionID/_ : integer, _/clientID/_ : integer)}
Outside of any box:
  Person : {(_PersonID_ : integer, FirstName : string, LastName : string)}
  Constants : {(_ID_ : integer, Name : string, Value : string)}
  PersonCategory : {(_/PersonID/_ : integer, _category_ : string)}

Foreign keys
  Member.PersonID -> Person.PersonID
  LogEntry.concernsPersonID -> Person.PersonID
  LogEntry.performedByPersonID -> Person.PersonID
  LogEntry.clientID -> Client.clientID
  LogEntry.(InvoiceNbr, DateOfIssue) -> Invoice.(InvoiceNbr, DateOfIssue)
  LogEntry.BookingID -> PurchaseOrder.BookingID
  LogEntry.ArticleCode -> SaleUnit.ArticleCode
  SpecialOffer.ArticleCode -> SaleUnit.ArticleCode
  Article.ArticleCode -> SaleUnit.ArticleCode
  Shopper.PersonID -> Person.PersonID
  Shopper.clientID -> Client.clientID
  Merchant.clientID -> Client.clientID
  PurchaseOrder.(InvoiceNbr, DateOfIssue) -> Invoice.(InvoiceNbr, DateOfIssue)
  CreditCard.clientID -> Client.clientID
  PhoneContact.clientID -> Client.clientID
  CreditCardOpt..OptionID -> PaymentOption.OptionID
  CreditCardOpt..CardNbr -> CreditCard.CardNbr
  PayOnDeliveryOpt..OptionID -> PaymentOption.OptionID
  PayOnDeliveryOpt..ContactID -> PhoneContact.ContactID
  SalesDiscount.BookingID -> PurchaseOrder.BookingID
  BookingItem.BookingID -> PurchaseOrder.BookingID
  BookingItem.ArticleCode -> SaleUnit.ArticleCode
  LogDetail.SessionID -> LogEntry.SessionID
  PersonCategory.PersonID -> Person.PersonID
  Member_partOf_InventoryMgmt.Team.PersonID -> Member.PersonID
  Member_partOf_InventoryMgmt.Team.TeamID -> InventoryMgmt.Team.TeamID
  InventoryMgmt.Team_updates_SaleInventoryItem.TeamID -> InventoryMgmt.Team.TeamID
  InventoryMgmt.Team_updates_SaleInventoryItem.ItemID -> SaleInventoryItem.ItemID
  SaleInventoryItem_partOf_SaleUnit.ItemID -> SaleInventoryItem.ItemID
  SaleInventoryItem_partOf_SaleUnit.ArticleCode -> SaleUnit.ArticleCode
  SpecialOffer_requires_SpecialCondition.ArticleCode -> SpecialOffer.ArticleCode
  SpecialOffer_requires_SpecialCondition.ConditionID -> SpecialCondition.ConditionID
  chooses.BookingID -> PurchaseOrder.BookingID
  chooses.OptionID -> PaymentOption.OptionID
  chooses.clientID -> Client.clientID

Unique (alternate keys)
  Shopper.clientID
  Merchant.MerchantID
  PurchaseOrder.(InvoiceNbr, DateOfIssue)
  chooses.(BookingID, clientID)
  chooses.(BookingID, OptionID)

Allowed values
  SaleUnit.category in {Article, Special offer}
  Client.category in {Shopper, Merchant}
  PaymentOption.category in {Credit card opt., Pay on delivery opt.}
  PersonCategory.category in {Member, Shopper}

Not enforced by the schema
  each Member has, in part of, Inventory mgmt. team: at least 1
  each Sale unit has, in part of, Sale inventory item: at least 1
  each Purchase order has, in contains, Booking item: at least 1
  each Invoice has, in encompasses, Purchase order: at least 1
  each Log entry has, in has, Log detail: at least 1

Decisions
  Generalisation Person ← Member, Shopper (co): (1) Multiple relations + categorisation relation
  Generalisation Client ← Shopper, Merchant (cd): (1) Multiple relations + categorisation attribute
  Generalisation Sale unit ← Article, Special offer (cd): (1) Multiple relations + categorisation attribute
  Generalisation Payment option ← Credit card opt., Pay on delivery opt. (cd): (1) Multiple relations + categorisation attribute
  Relationship chooses (1:1:1): Purchase order – Payment option – Client: Own relation, key: Payment option, Client
  Relationship encompasses (1:1): Purchase order – Invoice: Foreign key in Purchase order

Notes
  64 data type(s) were guessed from attribute names (set them with 'name : type').

